# GMP credentials for gmp.sh. Copy to .gmp.env, edit, then: chmod 600 .gmp.env
#
# Use a DEDICATED low-privilege GMP user, never the Greenbone 'admin' account. It needs only
# enough rights to modify the one credential object, and to start and read the tasks you scan
# with. You must create this GMP user yourself (gvmd --create-user, or via GSA);
# bootstrap/Initialize-GvmScanCredential.ps1 creates the CREDENTIAL OBJECT, not the user.
#
# This file is the single place the GMP password lives, and only root reads it: the relay that reads
# it runs as root, while the stub the RELAY account invokes holds nothing. (The relay account is the
# Linux account the Windows runner SSHes in as -- not the AD scan account, which never logs in here.)
# It must be 0600 AND root-owned; the relay refuses to source it otherwise, because it sources it as
# root.

# Either naming works; GMP_USER/GMP_PASS is what an existing deployment may already use.
#
# QUOTE THE PASSWORD. This file is not parsed as configuration -- it is SOURCED by /bin/sh as root, so
# an unquoted value is shell code: '&' backgrounds it, ';' ends the statement, '$' expands, '#'
# truncates, and a space makes the remainder a command. Single quotes keep it literal; double quotes
# still expand $ and backticks. Write a literal single quote as '\''.
GMP_USER='gvm-scan-automation'
GMP_PASS='change-me'
